    "number": 137,
    "title": "Show status first in the wall map with one context card",
    "body": "Refs #135\n\n## Summary\n\nThe wall map's default screen is now a status display, as the owner decided on 2026-09-24 (recorded in the issue and in ADR 0012).\n\n- The header holds Mode, the live readout and the connection pill. The Layout switch moves into a Layout group in the Options menu, where Coverage appears only while Project layout is active.\n- One context card replaces the selection and detail cards: the selected Line or Lines (or \"Waiting for a Line\" for a focused waiting task), then the task's title, status, project, elapsed time and Open in Codex link, then Locate. The task's title and project appear once outside the task tiles; in Classic the card carries no hint for a Line with a task, and in Project layout the hint states the reservation or Shared pool.\n- In Classic no reservation, half-swap or override control is shown. In Project layout the card adds the reservation select with a **Reserve** action (formerly \"Assign selected\"), Swap halves and the task's project override, through the same endpoints and pending-edit rules.\n- Clear selection is gone. Escape closes an open Options menu first, otherwise clears the selection; a click on empty wall canvas clears it too; both return focus to the wall heading. The Locate explanation appears only in Free.\n- A global `[hidden]` rule makes the `hidden` attribute win over layout rules, which also fixes the Numbers group from #78 staying visible when Prism is unavailable.\n\nThe bridge, the CLI `style` command and the integration-settings extension keep Project layout, reservations and overrides unchanged. No API, Python, state or device change.\n\n## OpenSpec and ADR\n\nChange `gh-135-context-card`, synchronized and archived at `openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-24-gh-135-context-card`: modified `wall-map-hierarchy` (default screen, Options groups, new context-card requirement), `wall-line-identification` (context card, Project-only reservation controls) and `wall-task-inspector` (context card, Project-only override). ADR `docs/decisions/0012-wall-map-status-first.md` records the decision; `0011` was taken by #136 on the same day.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Red before the change: the new `context_card_checks` module failed on the unchanged page with `Layout and Coverage have left the header: 3 !== 0`.\n- Green: the focused context-card check, then the full browser suite (green on the first full run at these bytes), `python3 scripts/check.py` with Node 24 (460 tests OK), `npm run check:workflow` (27 validated items, 0 failed) and `npm run test:workflow` (10 passed, 0 failed).\n- Suites that need the override or reservation controls now set Project layout in their fixtures; suites that cleared a selection press Escape.\n- Review screenshots in the `prism-wall-review` artifact: `context-card-classic.png`, `context-card-project.png`, `context-card-narrow.png`, plus the `hierarchy-*.png` set.\n\nComparison: base and merge-base `9e2c41313de3c69c32b8ddf5259b30517c14588f`; head `217e59c9599911f5630106d3e53db2eab8d5fa05`; `git diff 9e2c41313de3c69c32b8ddf5259b30517c14588f...217e59c9599911f5630106d3e53db2eab8d5fa05`; clean worktree `.local/worktrees/gh-135`.\n\nDelivery: direct coordinator implementation. Independent Standards and Specification reviews and current-head Depot CI are recorded in the PR comments.\n\nUI change: needs explicit human approval of this candidate before merge. Draft PR #116 edits the override's blur handler in the same file; this candidate keeps main's handler, and whichever merges second refreshes its comparison.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "state": "open",
