  {
    "number": 116,
    "title": "Reset recreated shared tasks and preserve Codex link focus",
    "body": "Refs https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/issues/218\nRefs #117\nCompanion: https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/238\n\nWhen Nanoleaf misses a session's removal and sees the same identity recreated, it currently retains the old task's manual project and effects. This companion requires snapshot 1.1 generation metadata and resets that task inside the existing projection transaction. Unchanged peers, global projects, reservations and native modes retain their behavior. The existing pinned 1.0 validator still validates the unchanged fields.\n\nA compatible Hub must be installed before activating this reader. A 1.0-only host reports unavailable without fallback. Source work changes no installed hooks, owner, Codex state or device.\n\nValidation: the regression failed with the retained manual project before the fix; focused generation/transport checks passed. The candidate on main `97b6b37fcbf93061adda9afab253517cee24996e` passed 462 Python tests, browser checks and workflow validation (18 main specs, one active change, 25 archived changes). The Hub owning-source harness exercised 41 shared fixtures plus removal, missed removal, restart, empty reconnect and unavailable retention. Renewed independent Standards and Specification source reviews found no actionable findings at `d3ae501413782d86aa5b3fadbbe9462d594af655`; all five current-head Depot jobs passed. The [review and CI receipt](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/codex-nanoleaf/pull/116#issuecomment-5821936903) records the fixed comparisons and check IDs.\n\nThe user also authorized the pre-existing focus repair in #117 after it failed hosted browser CI. Leaving Task project override now restores the saved value without invalidating the detail card. A forced unchanged poll preserves focus on Open in Codex, while lost eligibility still removes the link and returns focus to a surviving control. The regression failed before the fix; the full browser suite passed afterward. This restores the existing wall-task-inspector requirements, so the SDLC small-fix rule requires no additional OpenSpec delta.\n\nThis remains a draft. The user approved the current map focus behavior and the companion dashboard draft reset. Hub #218 retains separately authorized installation and visible Line acceptance. OpenSpec remains active pending those gates; archive, final reviews and merge are not complete. The installed trial also includes Hub #218's reopen-without-prompt observation.\n",
    "state": "open",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/jimmie-potts/codex-nanoleaf/pull/116",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-24T21:35:48Z",
    "draft": true,
    "head": {
      "label": "jimmie-potts:codex/gh-218-session-retirement",
      "ref": "codex/gh-218-session-retirement",
      "sha": "d3ae501413782d86aa5b3fadbbe9462d594af655",
      "user": {
        "login": "jimmie-potts",
        "id": 49133657,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTMzNjU3",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49133657?v=4",
        "gravatar_id": "",
